{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Ask a deep question.</b> Command after command without a connective vav, and like it התאחדי הימיני (Ezekiel 21:15). And the word שאלה is on the pattern of יי שמע (Daniel 9:19), as if he said: ask and deepen the request, that it be below or raised above. And R[abbi] said that the word העמק is also הגבה — a verb."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "'ורבי' most likely abbreviates ורבינו (and our Rabbi); resolved by inference from Ibn Ezra's standard usage."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:35.534908041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}